        "subject": "DRAFT LU-21180 lod: add kunit test for failure-domain checks",
        "message": "DRAFT LU-21180 lod: add kunit test for failure-domain checks\n\nExport lod_fd_check_ec_allowed() and lod_fd_check_flr_allowed() for\ndirect testing.\n\nAdd lustre/kunit/lod_fd_test.c, covering the failure-domain collision\nchecks used while selecting OSTs for EC and FLR (mirrored)\ncomponents, per Documentation/failure-domain.txt: a candidate OST\nmust not share a failure domain with another stripe already placed\nin the same raid set (or whole component, without overstriping), nor\nwith the linked data component's stripes when allocating parity\n(lod_fd_check_ec_allowed_test); nor with another stripe already\nplaced in the same component, nor with an overlapping component in a\ndifferent mirror (lod_fd_check_flr_allowed_test). Five mock_tgt\ntargets back these tests, with failure domains 1, 2, 1, 0 (none) and\n9, so collisions and the \"no domain\" passthrough can both be\nexercised.\n\nTest-Parameters: ignore\nSigned-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <rsahlberg@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: AGENT:claude-sonnet-5\nChange-Id: I9de39d0b224b4aa5be9af7931d87c029fe22c6c8\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
